{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{
  "readings": [
    {
      "local_id": "reading.complex_product_classification",
      "family": "modality",
      "subject": "Complex-product classification for distribution of SFC-authorised funds within the retained circular",
      "statement": "[TRUE_IS_SATISFIED] The question answered is whether, for a fund within this circular’s scope at the assessment time, a ground requiring complex-product treatment for distribution is established under this circular. True means that either the fund’s total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to at least 50% of its NAV, or an applicable SFC case-by-case complex-product designation exists. False means that neither ground applies, provided both grounds have been resolved on adequate evidence; it does not establish that the fund is non-complex under every other applicable rule. An unresolved exposure calculation or designation status remains unknown and must not be supplied as false. The scope comprises funds authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong, excluding listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs). Private market assets here comprise private credit and private equity, reached directly or indirectly. Exactly 50% triggers mandatory classification; no separate discretionary decision is stated as necessary at that threshold. Below 50%, footnote 7 places the classification assessment within the SFC’s holistic, case-by-case discretion. The SFC may designate such a fund after considering its aggregate exposures, investment strategy, portfolio composition, liquidity and risk profile, particular asset types and structures, and home-regulator distribution conditions; these factors are non-exhaustive and do not individually establish designation. Once classified, the fund is subject to the prevailing complex-product sale requirements, expressly including suitability irrespective of solicitation or recommendation. Fund managers must address the classification in their distributor selection and communications. The source supplies neither a particular fund’s exposure calculation nor its designation record, so no particular fund’s classification is decided here.",
      "distinction": "This is a classification-trigger predicate, not a Boolean finding of overall compliance, prohibition, licensing, or suitability. Mandatory classification at or above 50% is distinct from the SFC’s discretion to designate below 50%; discretion to make the designation does not make the resulting classification optional once an applicable designation exists. LAFs are excluded from this circular’s definition of Funds, rather than declared non-complex. The separate 15% direct-private-asset investment limit in footnote 1 does not replace the 50% combined-exposure threshold, excuse its application, or cap indirect exposures at 15%. Exposure-related disclosures, target-market duties, advertising requirements and authorisation scrutiny are separate from the classification trigger. Missing evidence of exposure or designation is an unresolved classification question, not evidence of an exemption or absence of designation.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u4.564",
          "quote": "This circular provides guidance to management companies of funds that are authorised by the SFC for offering to the public in Hong Kong (Funds)6 in this regard."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u21.3779",
          "quote": "A Fund will be considered as a complex product if its total direct and indirect exposures to private market assets amount to 50% or more of the Fund’s NAV."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u21.3779",
          "quote": "On a case-by-case basis, the SFC may also designate a Fund as a complex product, taking into account factors including, without limitation:"
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u29.4630",
          "quote": "In assessing whether the complex product designation is warranted7, the SFC will adopt a holistic approach taking into account the specific circumstances of the case."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u64.8910",
          "quote": "7 In cases where the Fund’s aggregate direct and indirect exposures to private market assets are less than 50% of the Fund’s NAV."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u63.8691",
          "quote": "6 Except for listed closed-ended alternative asset funds (LAFs)."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u32.4805",
          "quote": "including but not limited to ensuring the suitability of the Fund for its investors irrespective of whether solicitation or recommendation is involved."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u58.7778",
          "quote": "1 Direct investments in/exposures to private assets fall within the investment limit of 15% of a Fund’s total net asset value (NAV) under 7.3 of the Code on Unit Trusts and Mutual Funds (UT Code)."
        },
        {
          "unit_id": "d4148dd852cee.u49.6955",
          "quote": "Fund managers are encouraged to consult the SFC at the earliest opportunity if they are in doubt regarding complex product classification of their Funds."
        }
      ],
      "assumptions": [
        "All facts refer to the same identified fund and assessment time. The retained text does not provide that time or establish the circular’s publication, commencement or transitional dates.",
        "The formalization encodes the circular’s classification grounds only. It does not calculate exposures, predict an SFC discretionary decision, or encode the full distribution requirements incorporated by reference.",
        "The exposure-threshold fact must be supplied from an adequately supported aggregate-exposure assessment. The source does not specify a complete look-through, valuation, netting, derivative-exposure or double-counting methodology, or resolve whether actual, permitted or intended exposure controls every assessment.",
        "The SFC-designation fact concerns an actual applicable designation, not the presence of risk factors or the possibility that the SFC could designate the fund. Neither silence nor an unsuccessful search alone establishes its absence.",
        "No prior reading was supplied. The uncertainties concerning exposure measurement, timing, external requirements and fund-specific evidence remain unresolved in this initial proposal."
      ],
      "questions": [
        "What fund and assessment date are at issue, and is the fund SFC-authorised for public offering in Hong Kong and outside the LAF exclusion?",
        "What contemporaneous evidence establishes aggregate direct and indirect private-market exposure relative to NAV, and what measurement and look-through methodology governs that assessment?",
        "Does an applicable SFC case-by-case designation exist, and what are its effective date, scope and any subsequent changes?",
        "Does the governing classification practice assess actual holdings, permitted investment limits, intended exposure or a combination, and how are temporary threshold crossings treated?"
      ],
